MerkleAdapterHotPaths
├── when the computed payout is zero
│   ├── it avoids storage writes and preserves pending demand before release
│   ├── it avoids storage writes and preserves released liquidity for a zero request
│   ├── it preserves accounting through public deallocation and reverting simulation
│   └── it still rejects invalid NAV through the public delegator
├── when liquidity has been released
│   ├── it simulates without committing transfers and meters the public return and sweep
│   └── it still sweeps released liquidity when the initial requested amount is zero
└── when an approved account action pushes cash
    ├── it meters the transfer while protecting reserved cash and rejecting an excess push
    └── it meters a zero push while preserving accounting and emitting its event
